          text="Documented: the 7th Indiana, by Wadsworth's command, took position on the hill east of Gettysburg and immediately began a temporary breastwork; during the night an enemy force tried to penetrate the line and was driven off, and Sergeant Hussey took a Confederate lieutenant (T1-179); the 6th Wisconsin reported 'in open field on Culp's Hill'. Not documented: digging with a dozen spades shared among many, trees felled for logs (the felling of logs and the use of cord-wood is documented for the XII Corps works on Jul 2 only), and lantern or moon light. Computed: the moon stood 10 degrees high at 21:00 and 18.5 degrees at 22:00, 98.9 percent lit, with the cloud over it uncertain (T1-190).",
